# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dist/ is generated end-to-end from src/ by build/build_objs.py — never edit it
# by hand, and never commit it. Cut releases by building and attaching the ZIP.
dist/

# release/ is generated end-to-end by the build/ tooling (make_release.py +
# make_exe.py + make_allzip.py): the payload, the four per-platform bundles, and
# the All-Platforms zip all land here — never edit by hand, never commit it.
release/

# ── Local scratch (never committed) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendored third-party mods (Real Wings — someone else's assets, ~2 GB), old
# build snapshots, and anything else transient. Nothing here is an input to the
# build: patch_realwings.py locates the *installed* mod inside X-Plane itself.
.scratch/
.claude/
.vscode/
docs/
# Sim logs — symlinks into the live X-Plane install, for tailing.
Log.txt
XPPython3Log.txt

# ── Agent / editor cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CLAUDE.md
*.claude.md

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Native plugin (.xpl) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The X-Plane SDK is a third-party download (developer.x-plane.com), not ours to
# commit; CMake build tree is generated. See src/native/README.md.
src/native/SDK/
src/native/build/
src/native/build-dev/
# The SDK-free tree: `cmake -DPHOTON_CORE_ONLY=ON` builds photoncore,
# photoncore_tests and photon-installer with no X-Plane SDK present, which is what
# CI uses for the installer and what a contributor without the SDK can still run.
src/native/build-core/
# The GUI tree: `cmake -DPHOTON_GUI=ON` builds photon-installer with the Slint
# front-end. Its own tree because that configure downloads and compiles Slint from
# source (Rust), which is minutes of work nobody wants to redo by toggling a flag
# in a shared tree. See docs/installer_gui_plan.md.
src/native/build-gui/
# The dev-tools tree: `cmake -DPHOTON_TOOLS=ON` adds photon-lit-studio, which
# pulls in Dear ImGui and a Win32/GL backend that nothing else builds. Its own
# tree so a tools build never leaves ImGui objects in the tree CI reuses.
src/native/build-tools/

# ⚠ ToLiss's OWN stock textures, harvested locally by `photon-lit-studio harvest`
# so the tuning window can load them from a dropdown. THEY ARE PAYWARE AND NOT
# OURS TO REDISTRIBUTE — unlike reference/gus/, which is vendored with permission
# and says so. This repository is public and GPLv3, so only the README (which
# explains how to regenerate the folder in one command) is tracked.
reference/toliss/*
!reference/toliss/README.md
